1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,520
Believe in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,677
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,800
We live in wonderland.

26
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:53,937
Princess Vivi.

27
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:58,040
You see, this desert
is where. Ah! You die!

28
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:04,740
Potter!

29
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,180
Oh, no.

30
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:22,440
You see, you two can't get away, swan!

31
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:30,280
You hear me?

32
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:31,989
There's no escape for you!

33
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,197
Just give up now! Okay?

34
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:38,045
I'm going to trample you both
with all the grace of a ballerina!

35
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:42,970
Cotton!

36
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,617
You saved my life!

37
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,465
You're in no shape to be
running like this now!

38
00:02:58,880 --> 00:02:59,710
No!

39
00:02:59,793 --> 00:03:02,297
If you go straight, we'll
be cornered on the stairway!

40
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:03,640
Folks, listen to me!

41
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:06,056
Just give it up and stop right there!

42
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,900
Let me off here!

43
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,493
I'm going to fight him!

44
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:14,537
What are you doing?

45
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,738
That way's a cliff!

46
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,460
What are you doing?

47
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,180
You can't be serious!

48
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:32,011
That duck is actually running
up the sheer face of a cliff?

49
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,757
Dumb duck! Nice try,

50
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:49,252
but now you'll fall back down here and
my ballet Kenpo will finish you off!

51
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:57,460
How'd he do that?

52
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,160
Karoo, that's amazing! You flew!

53
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,650
Surely Mr.

54
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,357
Two won't be able to
follow us at this point.

55
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:09,920
That was a cute little
move, Duck, but it's no use!

56
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,260
There's nothing I can't do!

57
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:17,186
With the help of my incredible ballet
compo, I can renovate right up this cliff!

58
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:33,497
Arun, do you think you can make
it through the battlefield?

59
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,197
We'll never be able to find
Koza in all this confusion,

60
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,817
so we'll look for Chaka instead.

61
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,637
We need to reach the royal palace.

62
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:42,997
And we have to make it before the rebel
army reaches the center of the city.

63
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:43,910
We must!

64
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,990
Oh my!

65
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:49,440
I'm here!

66
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,940
A straight bullet, oh no!

67
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:03,490
Karoo!

68
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,720
Phoebe is our friend too, Kokoro!

69
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,650
Gotcha!

70
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,330
Karoo!

71
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:36,910
Karoo!

72
00:05:36,993 --> 00:05:37,823
Karoo!

73
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:55,560
Just give up!

74
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,800
I told you, it's no use!

75
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,000
All right.

76
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:10,320
Stay out of my way, Dock!

77
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:12,757
And maybe you won't get hurt, okay?

78
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,720
I...

79
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,200
WAAAAAAA! No, stop!

80
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,300
It's you guys.

81
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,737
Nice work there, Captain Karoo.

82
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:43,240
You did a damn good job.

83
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:48,240
Oh Sanji you're here.

84
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,197
At ease ducks.

85
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,580
You can stand down.

86
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:54,277
Now Vivi?

87
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,420
Don't you have a rebellion to stop?

88
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,020
Go on.

89
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:02,460
I'll take care of this creep.

90
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:10,717
So I take it you're that
ridiculous face changing freak huh?

91
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:13,720
You really should stay out of my way!

92
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,700
But first, just who are you?

93
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:17,580
Go on.

94
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,780
You guys, watch Karoo.

95
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:29,060
Oh, no!

96
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:30,720
She's getting away!

97
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:33,060
Oh, you gotta be kidding me!

98
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,480
Give me a break here!

99
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,717
Well, now you get to die!

100
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:41,388
I think I'll get started by having you
return our sharp-shoots prized goggles.

101
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:46,420
And that's just the beginning. Huh?

102
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:51,177
Hope you didn't think I would
be as easy to beat as him.

103
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:52,977
You're with the Straw Hats, huh?

104
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:56,720
Well, then, that must make
you the mysterious prince.

105
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:03,580
My name is Sanji, and I'm the
best cook in the entire ocean.

106
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:06,250
Cook?

107
00:08:06,333 --> 00:08:09,520
I happen to be a super
first-class top-rate cook as well.

108
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:14,557
But I use my skills to support an underworld
organization, not some useless kingdom.

109
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:16,977
You're not the only one
who knows the underworld.

110
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:19,160
I happen to be a cook and a pirate.

111
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,590
Hmm.

112
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:23,747
Well, then, this should
be quite interesting.

113
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,240
I'll make this clear.

114
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,541
Keep your hands off this country.

115
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:39,650
Chopper!

116
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:41,130
Chopper!

117
00:08:41,213 --> 00:08:42,043
Hey, Chopper!

118
00:08:42,126 --> 00:08:43,340
Come on, wake up!

119
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,480
Open your eyes!

120
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,571
Oh, Usopp, it looks like you're all right.

121
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,550
That's great.

122
00:08:49,633 --> 00:08:50,463
Don't be ridiculous.

123
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,377
You're the one we need to worry about.

124
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:53,695
No, it isn't serious.

125
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,617
So, this is all that's left of the Mr.

126
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:58,530
Four pair, huh?

127
00:08:58,613 --> 00:09:00,137
And here I came to help you.

128
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:02,777
I, the great Captain Usopp,
the champion of the seas,

129
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:05,777
the hero of the world, was going
to demonstrate my fighting skills.

130
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:08,057
by bravely coming to a friend's rescue.

131
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:08,970
Be careful.

132
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,737
They're still here waiting for us.

133
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,650
What?

134
00:09:11,733 --> 00:09:12,563
Why didn't you say so?

135
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
What was that?

136
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,357
How did that happen?

137
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,205
There's no one even out there.

138
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:27,357
That's because they're underground.

139
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:31,257
Miss Merry Christmas ate the mole mole
Devil Fruit and now she's a mole woman.

140
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,197
A mole woman?

141
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,960
The other one, Mr.

142
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:37,540
Four, is a fourth batter
and his dog's the pitcher.

143
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:39,250
What?

144
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:40,737
None of that Jabra jabber made any sense!

145
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:42,408
What the hell does it mean?

146
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:47,250
Look out!

147
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:49,690
Four!

148
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,880
Are you okay, Lusop?

149
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:16,157
Man, that was really close.

150
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,557
I'm glad you were there, Chopper.

151
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:19,758
What exactly was that thing, anyway?

152
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,520
Like I said, that's Mr. Four's thing.

153
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:23,975
He's a fourth batter.

154
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:26,264
He works together with his dog.

155
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:27,937
Which brings me back to my earlier point.

156
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:29,726
None of that makes any sense.

157
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:31,050
Ha!

158
00:10:31,133 --> 00:10:31,963
Look, he's over there!

159
00:10:32,046 --> 00:10:32,876
Huh?

160
00:10:32,959 --> 00:10:33,980
A dog?

161
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:37,590
Gah!

162
00:10:37,673 --> 00:10:39,220
What is that weird thing?

163
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:50,240
That's not good. What? Huh? What's that?

164
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,670
Gah!

165
00:10:53,753 --> 00:10:55,440
Here it comes! Not good!

166
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,057
Usopp, you have to get
away from there, quickly!

167
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:05,970
Hurry, now!

168
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:14,790
Usopp, no!

169
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,651
Are you all right, Usopp?

170
00:11:23,740 --> 00:11:24,916
Okay, one more time.

171
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,260
What is that?

172
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:29,097
The ball is a time bomb and explodes when

173
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:30,977
it's set to whether or
not it hits anything.

174
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:31,980
Basically, Mr.

175
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:34,697
Fork can calculate the time
needed and then hit the ball.

176
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:37,257
The ball will then explode
when its time is up.

177
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:40,037
I tried to catch one before it
exploded and throw it back at him,

178
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:42,037
but it's as heavy as a wrecking ball.

179
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:44,737
There's no way to catch it,
and it's impossible to throw.

180
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:45,757
The fact that Mr.

181
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:49,557
Fork can hit it with a bat at the
speed he does is absolutely incredible.

182
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:51,037
His strength is extraordinary.

183
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,649
It's beyond anything
I've ever seen before.

184
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:08,057
That bat of his just
knocked down a brick wall.

185
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:10,297
How much could that thing possibly weigh?

186
00:12:10,380 --> 00:12:13,320
Hey, Mr. Four! Mr. Four!

187
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,500
What are you doing, moron?

188
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:16,580
You moron!

189
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:18,957
Go and get him instead
of just standing there.

190
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,460
Come on, let him have it already. Go now!

191
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:22,560
Go on, moron!

192
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:23,490
Kill him!

193
00:12:23,573 --> 00:12:24,403
Smoke him!

194
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,677
Moron! Moron! Run!

195
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,590
Run!

196
00:12:27,673 --> 00:12:28,503
Run!

197
00:12:28,586 --> 00:12:29,416
Now! Do it now!

198
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,657
Over there, it's the mole woman.

199
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:34,916
She is a mole woman!

200
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:36,537
I haven't even changed yet!

201
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:38,220
You moron, you moron!

202
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,757
Chopper, you'll have to take it from here.

203
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,877
Do me a favor and have my body buried
and see what I've gone okay on.

204
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:44,957
You cowardly jerk!

205
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:47,477
You just got done saying
you had come here to help!

206
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,480
Look here, you!

207
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,157
How do you expect me to fight
against a freaky muscle man,

208
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:53,697
his weird dog-gun
hybrid, and a mole woman?

209
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:54,662
There's no way!

210
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:55,800
I'm a human.

211
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,537
Do you think you can understand that?

212
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,080
I'm a human too, jerk!

213
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,050
No, you're not.

214
00:13:00,133 --> 00:13:00,977
You're a big furry monster.

215
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:01,980
What about you?

216
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,041
Have you seen that nose of yours?

217
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:05,617
Anyway, his name is Lasso.

218
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,437
He's a gun that ate the dachshund
variety of the mutt-mutt fruit.

219
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:09,780
Are we clear?

220
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:12,617
Let me get this straight.

221
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,657
Are you saying that a
gun ate a Devil Fruit?

222
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:17,117
It's a new technique
here on the Grand Line.

223
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,847
Even inanimate objects
can eat a Devil Fruit.

224
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,310
Ha!

225
00:13:21,393 --> 00:13:22,223
You call that lying?

226
00:13:22,306 --> 00:13:24,237
If he was originally a gun,
how could he eat anything?

227
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,877
A gun can't even move on its own.

228
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:28,597
You're just making all of
this up, you mole-woman!

229
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:29,510
Shut up!

230
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,977
It's top secret anyway, and I wouldn't have
told you except for you're going to die.

231
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:34,577
A gun can't help it if it moves.

232
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:35,937
So there, there, there, there!

233
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:36,850
So there!

234
00:13:36,933 --> 00:13:37,817
Now isn't that right, Mr.

235
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:38,730
Four?

236
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:40,010
Mm-hmm.

237
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,617
Anyway, like I was saying,
you're gonna die here.

238
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:46,537
You have no hope of escaping now
that you've entered our territory.

239
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:47,450
No, nuh-uh.

240
00:13:47,533 --> 00:13:48,363
No hope at all.

241
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,357
You should enjoy this.

242
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:53,322
Welcome to a territory we
call Mole Hill Block 4.

243
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,190
Look!

244
00:13:59,273 --> 00:14:02,120
Now she's turning into a
mole-woman thing for real!

245
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:09,500
A penguin? A penguin! I'm a mole!

246
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:10,561
Now you shut up!

247
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:16,119
She's underground!

248
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:18,817
Now's my chance!

249
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:19,730
Wait, hey!

250
00:14:19,813 --> 00:14:21,855
You can handle it from here, I'm sure!

251
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:25,420
Watch out, who's up!

252
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:28,100
It's missed!

253
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,320
Close! Four!

254
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,420
Oh no!

255
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:36,660
Usopp, look, it's above you! Huh?

256
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,620
It's a fly ball! Ha!

257
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:39,840
No problem!

258
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:43,787
Looks like their cleanup batter
can't clean up very well, huh?

259
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:45,390
How sad!

260
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:47,932
I can dodge this one with my eyes closed!

261
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:49,730
Spinball!

262
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,660
Look out behind you!

263
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,837
He's fourth in our lineup
for a reason, moron!

264
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:01,685
You haven't seen anything yet!

265
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:26,538
They're over there!

266
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:29,375
How did you two have the time to move?

267
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,500
You changed form!

268
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,282
All right, so you're a zon-type!

269
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:40,246
And I was thinking you were just
a normal person all this time!

270
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:42,937
Usopp, we have no choice
but to keep moving.

271
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:45,057
If we stop for a second, we're dead.

272
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:45,970
I get it.

273
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:50,551
If we stand still, then we're just
sending ducks for them to keep firing at.

274
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,242
Here they come!

275
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:09,066
If I can get to that guy
and knock him down...

276
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:11,460
Just hold on!

277
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:16,255
The game isn't going to be any fun
if we don't have a batter, now is it?

278
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:21,750
Jumper!

279
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,774
Oh, well, at least I can still do that.

280
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:29,830
Huh?

281
00:16:29,913 --> 00:16:30,820
Dare we mole?

282
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:33,870
That's it!

283
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:38,590
Damn.

284
00:16:38,673 --> 00:16:41,757
If they keep running away through these
mole tunnels, even if I use a rumble ball?

285
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:44,605
I won't have enough time
to do any real damage.

286
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:47,950
Hey.

287
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:49,330
Where is he?

288
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:51,297
We're missing one of them!

289
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:53,177
Where's the ugly guy with
the long nose we're off to?

290
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:54,090
Where is he?

291
00:16:54,173 --> 00:16:55,003
Where?

292
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:57,773
Yeah, I don't see Usopp around anywhere.

293
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:58,910
What's the matter?

294
00:16:58,993 --> 00:17:00,372
You guys lose something?

295
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:03,760
Where are you?

296
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,960
Where did you go?

297
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:07,240
Wait, is he?

298
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:10,576
Yeah, so kind of you to dig
all these tunnels, really.

299
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,042
You do realize,

300
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:16,474
though, that you're not the only one
who can crawl around inside of them.

301
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,070
Usopp!

302
00:17:19,153 --> 00:17:20,400
You sneaky little rat!

303
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:22,778
You were hiding in one of the holes!

304
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:33,950
Whoa!

305
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:38,540
Mr. Fork!

306
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,310
What?

307
00:17:44,393 --> 00:17:46,897
It looks like he's
using a five-ton hammer!

308
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:50,568
How does a string bean like him
have the strength to do that?

309
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:58,580
That's a big hammer.

310
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:01,660
Who exactly is this long-nosed freak?

311
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,400
I am a traveler of the world's oceans,

312
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:11,177
a crusher of notorious monsters, beasts,
and foes, a sinker of countless ships,

313
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:14,117
a flattener of numberless
towns, trembling with fear.

314
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:17,259
People everywhere call me
the master of destruction.

315
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:21,206
I suggest that you take the time
to remember my name carefully.

316
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:25,120
I am Captain Usopp!

317
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,277
Wow, wow, wow!

318
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,337
Awesome, awesome, awesome!

319
00:18:29,420 --> 00:18:30,457
Yes, yes, thank you very much.

320
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:31,457
That's nothing really.

321
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:32,897
I'll be signing autographs later.

322
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:33,810
That was amazing.

323
00:18:33,893 --> 00:18:35,397
I thought you were useless up until now.

324
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,310
Hey!

325
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:39,200
Mr. Thor!

326
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:41,980
He isn't moving.

327
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:44,321
Could I really hit him that hard?

328
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,120
No, it doesn't matter.

329
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:48,297
This is my chance to beat them both.

330
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:49,480
I have to take it.

331
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,620
Your turn, Penguin!

332
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:55,140
Now you'll feel the wrath
of my five-ton hammer!

333
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:59,457
Ahhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh
Face my ooze up!

334
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:00,370
Down!

335
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,220
She escaped.

336
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,920
Where are you, Penguin?

337
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:06,357
I told you I'm a mole,
not a Penguin, moro!

338
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,740
Now I see you!

339
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:15,920
Rubber baby boom.

340
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:23,250
Damn!

341
00:19:23,333 --> 00:19:25,085
You're everywhere, mole-woman!

342
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:26,250
Ha!

343
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:29,097
Hey, you missed me, so what's
the point of that big hammer?

344
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,000
If you can't manage to hit me!

345
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,439
Let me tell you something, Penguin.

346
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:38,277
I'm sure you've heard by now
that a good number of your

347
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,595
fellow Baroque Works agents
have been eliminated by us.

348
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:46,280
But the truth is, it was all me. No!

349
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:47,370
You did all that!

350
00:19:47,453 --> 00:19:52,140
In addition to that, I command 8,000 men!

351
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,140
That's awesome!

352
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,580
Five tons! Awesome! Five tons! Awesome!

353
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:07,380
Five tons! Awesome! Five tons! Awesome!

354
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:09,780
Five tons! Awesome!

355
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,800
He has to wake up now?

356
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:16,800
He survived being hit
by a five-ton hammer?

357
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:18,680
What kind of monster is he?

358
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:21,646
Yeah, he doesn't even
have a bump on his head!

359
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:26,315
He took a direct blow to the head
from a five-ton hammer, and he's okay?

360
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,480
Why is that?

361
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:40,680
You mean that thing was
a fake this whole time?

362
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:42,460
Of course it was!

363
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,597
You think I can really lift five tons?

364
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:46,897
I stopped trying after just ten pounds!

365
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:48,477
This is a model I made!

366
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:52,854
It's only a couple of frying pans tied
to a stick and covered with paper.

367
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:00,000
Why, you!

368
00:21:00,340 --> 00:21:02,516
You tricked me with a piece of paper!

369
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,080
No more mercy for you!

370
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,940
Mole swimming! Mole fishing!

371
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:13,740
She's gone underground into
the mole tunnels again!

372
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,821
Watch out for the holes, chopper!

373
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,737
What's she planning this time?

374
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:22,077
Moving around underground is just
like swimming in a pool to me!

375
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:23,748
You can't escape this time!

376
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:28,510
Pool?

377
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:35,100
Now this is bad.

378
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,760
Oh, no! What's up?

379
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,917
Mr. Four! Lasso!

380
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:48,824
Go ahead and take care of that
reindeer man over there, would ya?

381
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:51,676
Let's show them your 400 base knocks!

382
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,040
It's no use.

383
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:03,144
There's no way I can
handle an attack like this.

384
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,792
It's all or nothing now.

385
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:07,337
I have to think up a way to beat this guy.

386
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:09,760
And quickly, before he kills us both!

387
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:13,110
Rumble!

388
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:20,080
Brain pulling!

389
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,180
Let's go!

390
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:38,700
Where's Chopper?

391
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,240
Chopper.

392
00:22:45,980 --> 00:22:49,098
You don't have time to be
worried about someone else!

393
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,940
Here comes my mole banana!

394
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:59,257
Hey now! What are you doing?

395
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:01,737
It's poor form to go
after that spot on a guy!

396
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:02,717
Stop your whining!

397
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:04,212
You're alive, aren't ya?

398
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:05,440
Mole banana!

399
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:12,950
Perfect.

400
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:15,057
There's part of a wall there.

401
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:17,417
If I keep running at this
speed and she follows me,

402
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:20,417
she'll run into the part of
the wall that's under the sand.

403
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,500
And she'll crash really hard, too.

404
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,780
Banana! Banana!

405
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:32,354
Now it's time to split your
head in two, stupid penguin!

406
00:23:55,420 --> 00:23:57,060
What's up?

407
00:24:07,020 --> 00:24:08,420
Four...

408
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:36,270
Yeah.

409
00:24:41,020 --> 00:24:41,877
Got crushed, huh?

410
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:44,437
Well, it serves you right,
you stupid old penguin woman!

411
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:45,350
I'm a mole!

412
00:24:45,433 --> 00:24:46,554
I'm a mole, you moron!

413
00:24:47,540 --> 00:24:48,370
Ah!

414
00:24:48,453 --> 00:24:49,283
Go to the highway!

415
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:51,700
Oh, come on!

416
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:54,400
Oh, what are you doing? Let me go!

417
00:24:55,020 --> 00:24:55,961
Stop it already!

418
00:24:56,100 --> 00:24:57,577
This is too dangerous to do out here!

419
00:24:57,660 --> 00:24:59,497
If you're not careful,
we'll run into something!

420
00:24:59,580 --> 00:25:00,410
Ah!

421
00:25:00,493 --> 00:25:01,323
Like that wall in front of you!

422
00:25:01,406 --> 00:25:03,960
Look ahead! A wall! A wall! No!

423
00:25:04,220 --> 00:25:06,040
I'm too young to die!

424
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:08,120
Oh, mole in bed!

425
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:12,790
Ah!

426
00:25:18,620 --> 00:25:19,780
I got it!

427
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:21,940
I see your weakness now! Oh?

428
00:25:30,260 --> 00:25:31,090
Ooh!

429
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:49,070
Usopp!

430
00:25:49,153 --> 00:25:50,014
Usopp, can you get up?

431
00:25:50,100 --> 00:25:51,140
Come on, Usopp!

432
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:55,006
Stay away from the fall
in all the halls, too!

433
00:25:56,260 --> 00:25:58,789
You don't have to tell
me twice, I'm going!

434
00:25:59,980 --> 00:26:00,810
Hurry up!

435
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:03,780
What exactly are those morons doing now?

436
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:28,400
What's that?

437
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:43,959
And that's the molehill's weakness.

438
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:48,802
All of the tunnels are connected
to each other in one big network.

439
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:50,550
Oh?

440
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:53,430
Yeah?

441
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:08,920
They're alive!

442
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:10,360
This isn't good.

443
00:27:10,740 --> 00:27:14,211
My Rumble Ball's effectiveness
is already half gone by now!

444
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:20,000
No more! Huh?

445
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:22,080
No more of this!

446
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,217
I don't want to die in this place!

447
00:27:24,300 --> 00:27:25,130
Usopp, wait!

448
00:27:25,213 --> 00:27:26,043
No way!

449
00:27:26,126 --> 00:27:26,956
I'm out of here!

450
00:27:27,039 --> 00:27:27,869
I've had it!

451
00:27:27,952 --> 00:27:28,797
There's no way to beat these two!

452
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:31,357
Not when they're still
alive after that explosion!

453
00:27:31,440 --> 00:27:35,264
Running away from them isn't going
to do any good, don't you see?

454
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:37,190
Usopp!

455
00:27:37,273 --> 00:27:39,001
The blue nose is right, you know!

456
00:27:41,480 --> 00:27:43,833
That was quite a little stunt, you bull!

457
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:45,437
After doing something like that,

458
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:48,517
we're not gonna just let you
run away like nothing happened!

459
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:49,940
Oh no, Lucy!

460
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:55,990
Well,

461
00:27:56,073 --> 00:27:57,397
I guess with the captain
who's so pathetic,

462
00:27:57,480 --> 00:28:00,598
it's no surprise that the
rest of the crew's useless.

463
00:28:05,460 --> 00:28:06,290
Captain?

464
00:28:06,373 --> 00:28:07,377
Wait, are you...

465
00:28:07,460 --> 00:28:09,107
are you talking about Luffy?

466
00:28:09,500 --> 00:28:11,417
If you're talking about the Straw Hat Kid,

467
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:13,737
that idiot was killed a
little while ago by the boss.

468
00:28:13,820 --> 00:28:14,702
What a shocker.

469
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:18,295
And now the rebellion has
started and is well underway.

470
00:28:18,580 --> 00:28:21,815
Well, I guess you picked the
wrong people to mess with.

471
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:31,300
She said Luffy is dead.

472
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:37,120
Don't you dare lie to us!

473
00:28:38,520 --> 00:28:40,637
Don't lie to us, you dirty mole woman!

474
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:42,017
We aren't gonna listen to you!

475
00:28:42,100 --> 00:28:43,857
There's no way Luffy can be dead!

476
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:44,817
Do you hear me?

477
00:28:44,900 --> 00:28:47,480
He'd never lose to that alligator bastard!

478
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,257
And what makes you think
that scrawny little captain

479
00:28:50,340 --> 00:28:52,577
of yours can even last five
seconds against our boss,

480
00:28:52,660 --> 00:28:53,797
you stupid long nose?

481
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:57,257
Because someday he's going to
become the king of the pirates.

482
00:28:57,340 --> 00:29:00,634
So there's no chance that he
would let himself die here.

483
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:05,420
Did you hear that, Mr. Four?

484
00:29:05,540 --> 00:29:06,877
He'll be the pirate king.

485
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:08,400
Pie king, pie king.

486
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:12,849
That's the stupidest
thing I've ever heard.

487
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:20,140
I have...

488
00:29:20,680 --> 00:29:21,757
King of the pirates!

489
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:23,677
Only idiots like you and
your pathetic friends

490
00:29:23,760 --> 00:29:26,177
will believe a ridiculous story like that!

491
00:29:26,260 --> 00:29:28,837
I'm glad that pathetic
captain of yours is dead!

492
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:31,567
He was a moron who didn't
know his own place!

493
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:32,837
He was a rod!

494
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:33,940
A rod!

495
00:29:43,540 --> 00:29:44,580
Jumper, listen!

496
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,440
A real man?

497
00:29:49,620 --> 00:29:52,260
It's about time you died, long-nosed!

498
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:54,520
Hill Highway!

499
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:57,277
Listen to me, a real man,

500
00:29:57,360 --> 00:30:01,242
no matter how terrifying or hideous
or corrupt his enemy might be!

501
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:04,760
I'll see you in hell,
Ron, you long-nosed Ron!

502
00:30:06,740 --> 00:30:08,540
Oh, no, him back!

503
00:30:10,620 --> 00:30:11,560
You okay?

504
00:30:11,980 --> 00:30:13,800
No, no matter.

505
00:30:14,580 --> 00:30:18,040
How's live the chance a
real man will still fight?

506
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:21,320
Mr. Four!

507
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:24,160
You're up!

508
00:30:24,300 --> 00:30:26,006
Now take your betting stance!

509
00:30:26,460 --> 00:30:28,040
Ready your four-ton bet!

510
00:30:29,600 --> 00:30:30,880
This is it!

511
00:30:31,220 --> 00:30:32,420
Mole hill!

512
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:44,020
Intersection number four!

513
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:46,230
Gah!

514
00:30:48,860 --> 00:30:50,040
What's up now?

515
00:31:04,820 --> 00:31:07,857
The waker always weak, even
if they pretend they're not!

516
00:31:07,940 --> 00:31:08,770
How sad!

517
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:12,120
Damn you!

518
00:31:13,660 --> 00:31:15,540
What did you do to him?

519
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:29,580
There are times when a real
man must stay and fight

520
00:31:30,100 --> 00:31:32,900
instead of running, no matter what.

521
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:37,160
You're still standing?

522
00:31:37,740 --> 00:31:38,960
Like now.

523
00:31:39,940 --> 00:31:45,840
When a friend's true dream is
laughed at by someone No way!

524
00:31:46,020 --> 00:31:47,617
You were hit in the head with a bat that

525
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:51,180
weighs four tons You shouldn't
even be alive, you damn Ron!

526
00:31:51,540 --> 00:31:53,677
You shouldn't, no you shouldn't,
shouldn't even be alive,

527
00:31:53,760 --> 00:31:57,407
no way What sort of sneaky trick
are you using this time, huh?

528
00:31:59,180 --> 00:32:00,880
Luffy is not dead.

529
00:32:01,740 --> 00:32:05,240
He's going to be King
of the Pirates someday!

530
00:32:07,900 --> 00:32:09,340
I know he will!

531
00:32:11,640 --> 00:32:16,900
That is one day that I will never
let you laugh at! Never! Ha!

532
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:19,857
I guess the Long Nose hasn't
learned his lesson yet.

533
00:32:19,940 --> 00:32:21,140
Let's go again, Mr.

534
00:32:21,260 --> 00:32:22,090
Firehorn!

535
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:27,725
